** {{audio|en|en-us-alternate-verb.ogg|a=US}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Happening by turns; one following the other in [[succession]] of time or place; first one and then the other (repeatedly).
#: {{syn|en|{{qualifier|North America}} [[alternating]]}}
#* {{RQ:Pope Essay on Criticism|passage=And bid '''alternate''' passions fall and rise}}
## {{lb|en|heraldry}} Alternating; (of e.g. a pair of tinctures which a charge is coloured) succeeding in turns, or (relative to the field) [[counterchanged]].
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1925|title=The Jewish Encyclopedia: Chazars-Dreyfus Case|page=128
|text=Goldschmidt (Austria; creation July 27, 1862): [...] party, argent and gules, an eagle of '''alternate''' colors, [...]}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} Designating the members in a series, which regularly intervene between the members of another series, as the odd or even numbers of the numerals; every other; every second.
#: {{co|en|the '''alternate''' members 1, 3, 5, 7, etc.}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly|North America}} [[other|Other]]; [[alternative]].
#: {{ux|en|Hyperlinked text is displayed in '''alternate''' color in a Web browser.}}
#: {{ux|en|He lives in an [[alternate universe|'''alternate''' universe]] and an '''alternate''' reality.}}
#: {{ux|en|Let's take an '''alternate''' route to avoid the [[traffic jam]].}}
# {{lb|en|botany|of leaves}} Distributed singly at different heights of the stem, and at equal intervals as respects angular divergence<ref>{{R:Gray Botany}}</ref>
#: {{ux|en|Many trees have '''alternate''' leaf arrangement (e.g. birch, oak and mulberry).}}

====Usage notes====
* According to the Oxford Learner's Dictionaries, the term is used chiefly in North America for the "other" sense, while "[[alternative]]" is used in both North America and Britain.<ref>{{R:Oxford Learner's Dictionaries}}</ref>

